      "writtenOn": "2021-07-19T20:42:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Still active: It looks like we fail immediately if any call to parameter() returns an unpopulated optional.\n\nIt seems like we only need `parameterPointers` and could avoid the existence of the `parameters` array entirely.\n\nThis was marked Done before but it\u0027s back.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 318,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 320,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "7bc300ca72107799407460bbbe595b2d4357dc3a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2159bb28_05a94c8b",
        "filename": "src/sksl/SkSLDSLParser.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 52
      },
      "lineNbr": 320,
      "author": {
        "id": 5640
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-07-20T19:23:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Looks like I accidentally blew part of the fix away sometime during the endless stream of rebases and merges.\n\nJust to be clear, I believe failing immediately is the correct behavior; the issue was that we were still then passing around optionals even though we had established by that point that we had a value.\n\nThe earlier problems re. parameterPointers had to do with taking pointers into an array, then modifying the array which would potentially invalidate those pointers. I fixed that by delaying taking the pointers until the array is finished. Unfortunately we still need parameterPointers (since that\u0027s the type of array DSLFunction() expects), and I don\u0027t see a way to reasonably do it without still maintaining the original parameters array - where would we be storing the DSLParameters that we\u0027re taking pointers to, if not in an array?",
      "parentUuid": "7f361893_87c427f8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 318,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 320,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "7bc300ca72107799407460bbbe595b2d4357dc3a",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
