      "message": "Agreed. Alternately, a different kind of repetition:\n\ncase TK_PLUS:\ncase TK_MINUS:\n...\n  if (!depth.increase()) { return nullopt; }\n  this-\u003enextToken();\n  expr \u003d this-\u003eunaryExpression();\n  if (!expr) { return nullopt; }\n  switch (this-\u003epeek().fKind) {\n    case TK_PLUS: return {{+std::move(**expr)}};\n    ...\n  }\n  \nThat repeats the cases in the nested switch, but makes it clear to the compiler that we only want one copy of the setup chunk, and is still fewer net lines of code, too.",
